WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.400
Welcome. This class turns multi-agent
handoffs into explicit, testable

2
00:00:06.400 --> 00:00:12.800
transfers. You will decide between
delegation and control transfer, build

3
00:00:12.800 --> 00:00:19.200
a versioned packet, minimize context and
authority, require acceptance and

4
00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:25.600
return evidence, and test failures without
depending on one provider

5
00:00:25.600 --> 00:00:32.000
framework.

6
00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:37.429
First decide whether control should move.
In delegation, the parent

7
00:00:37.429 --> 00:00:42.857
remains responsible for the user-facing
outcome. It gives a specialist

8
00:00:42.857 --> 00:00:48.286
a bounded subtask, receives a typed
artifact, validates that artifact,

9
00:00:48.286 --> 00:00:53.714
and performs final synthesis. Research,
classification, generation, and review

10
00:00:53.714 --> 00:00:59.143
often fit this pattern. In a handoff, the
specialist becomes

11
00:00:59.143 --> 00:01:04.571
the active agent and continues the next
phase under its

12
00:01:04.571 --> 00:01:10.000
own instructions. Use that transfer when
the specialist must interact

13
00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:15.429
directly, the phase has a distinct
responsibility, and the transition

14
00:01:15.429 --> 00:01:20.857
is understandable to the user. A tool call
that invokes

15
00:01:20.857 --> 00:01:26.286
another agent may implement either
behavior, so SDK syntax is

16
00:01:26.286 --> 00:01:31.714
not the definition. Name the control owner
before and after

17
00:01:31.714 --> 00:01:37.143
the operation, who may speak to the user,
who validates

18
00:01:37.143 --> 00:01:42.571
the result, and exactly when control
returns. If those answers

19
00:01:42.571 --> 00:01:48.000
are unclear, keep the parent active.

20
00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:53.692
Build a packet, not a conversation dump. A
curriculum triage

21
00:01:53.692 --> 00:01:59.385
agent routes four claims to a source
reviewer. The packet

22
00:01:59.385 --> 00:02:05.077
identifies the schema version, run and
parent span, sender and

23
00:02:05.077 --> 00:02:10.769
intended recipient role, routing reason,
user goal, accepted constraints, and

24
00:02:10.769 --> 00:02:16.462
four claims with source references. It
lists the current draft

25
00:02:16.462 --> 00:02:22.154
artifact, completed actions and
idempotency keys, unresolved questions,

26
00:02:22.154 --> 00:02:27.846
allowed read and comment actions, denied
publish and delete actions,

27
00:02:27.846 --> 00:02:33.538
a three-turn budget, success criteria, and
return states for review

28
00:02:33.538 --> 00:02:39.231
complete, evidence missing, or policy
blocked. The receiver validates required

29
00:02:39.231 --> 00:02:44.923
fields, freshness, recipient match,
contract version, and permitted authority

30
00:02:44.923 --> 00:02:50.615
before accepting. An incomplete packet is
rejected with a reason.

31
00:02:50.615 --> 00:02:56.308
This makes a transfer reproducible and
prevents conversational history from

32
00:02:56.308 --> 00:03:02.000
becoming an accidental, ambiguous
interface.

33
00:03:02.000 --> 00:03:07.250
Watch the reviewer validate two packets.
Packet A names the

34
00:03:07.250 --> 00:03:12.500
reviewer role, carries four sourced
claims, permits read and comment,

35
00:03:12.500 --> 00:03:17.750
denies publication, and defines three
return states. It is accepted.

36
00:03:17.750 --> 00:03:23.000
Packet B targets a publisher, omits
provenance, includes a broad

37
00:03:23.000 --> 00:03:28.250
credential, and has no return condition.
It is rejected before

38
00:03:28.250 --> 00:03:33.500
any model work begins. The rejection
records recipient mismatch, missing

39
00:03:33.500 --> 00:03:38.750
evidence, excessive authority, and an
unsupported terminal contract so the

40
00:03:38.750 --> 00:03:44.000
sender can repair or escalate
deliberately.

41
00:03:44.000 --> 00:03:49.571
Minimize what crosses the boundary. Do not
forward hidden reasoning,

42
00:03:49.571 --> 00:03:55.143
unrelated personal data, secrets, every
tool result, or the entire

43
00:03:55.143 --> 00:04:00.714
conversation merely because the parent saw
it. Select the facts,

44
00:04:00.714 --> 00:04:06.286
constraints, artifacts, and source labels
the recipient needs. Separate trusted

45
00:04:06.286 --> 00:04:11.857
instructions from quoted user material,
retrieved text, and other untrusted

46
00:04:11.857 --> 00:04:17.429
content. Preserve provenance so the
specialist can distinguish a verified

47
00:04:17.429 --> 00:04:23.000
fact from an unresolved claim. Then
re-evaluate authority for the

48
00:04:23.000 --> 00:04:28.571
recipient. Parent credentials do not flow
downhill. Resolve the recipient

49
00:04:28.571 --> 00:04:34.143
identity and tenant, issue a scoped
credential when needed, enforce

50
00:04:34.143 --> 00:04:39.714
object-level authorization, and deny tools
outside the assigned role. If

51
00:04:39.714 --> 00:04:45.286
the specialist changes the target, side
effect, data disclosure, or

52
00:04:45.286 --> 00:04:50.857
requested scope, require fresh approval. A
handoff may narrow authority.

53
00:04:50.857 --> 00:04:56.429
It must never silently widen it. Deleting
context is not

54
00:04:56.429 --> 00:05:02.000
enough if an overpowered credential still
allows unrelated action.

55
00:05:02.000 --> 00:05:06.933
Require acknowledgment on both sides. The
receiver either accepts the

56
00:05:06.933 --> 00:05:11.867
packet or rejects it with a typed reason
such as

57
00:05:11.867 --> 00:05:16.800
wrong recipient, missing provenance, stale
artifact, unsupported contract, or

58
00:05:16.800 --> 00:05:21.733
excessive permission. Acceptance records
the active agent, time, trace, packet

59
00:05:21.733 --> 00:05:26.667
hash, and granted budget. Return is also a
contract. It

60
00:05:26.667 --> 00:05:31.600
contains the outcome state, changed
artifacts, evidence produced, tool actions

61
00:05:31.600 --> 00:05:36.533
and postconditions, remaining uncertainty,
budget used, and requested next decision.

62
00:05:36.533 --> 00:05:41.467
The parent validates that result before
synthesis or another transfer.

63
00:05:41.467 --> 00:05:46.400
Bound repeated bounce-backs, recursive
delegation, and revision loops. Track

64
00:05:46.400 --> 00:05:51.333
depth and visited roles, cap retries, and
reject a transfer

65
00:05:51.333 --> 00:05:56.267
that would create a cycle beyond policy.
If no eligible

66
00:05:56.267 --> 00:06:01.200
recipient accepts, evidence is
unavailable, authority conflicts, or time

67
00:06:01.200 --> 00:06:06.133
expires, escalate the packet and failure
history to a human

68
00:06:06.133 --> 00:06:11.067
or deterministic failure path. Do not
guess, erase the rejection,

69
00:06:11.067 --> 00:06:16.000
or invent success.

70
00:06:16.000 --> 00:06:21.286
Keep the portable contract above provider
adapters. OpenAI's Agents SDK

71
00:06:21.286 --> 00:06:26.571
can represent handoffs as tools, attach
typed input, and filter

72
00:06:26.571 --> 00:06:31.857
history. Google ADK supplies workflow and
agent-team structures. Anthropic describes

73
00:06:31.857 --> 00:06:37.143
orchestrator-worker and
evaluator-optimizer patterns. These ideas

74
00:06:37.143 --> 00:06:42.429
overlap, but they do not promise identical
lifecycle, context, guardrail,

75
00:06:42.429 --> 00:06:47.714
or authority behavior. Define product
invariants independently: correct

76
00:06:47.714 --> 00:06:53.000
recipient, minimal context, unchanged or
narrower authority, continuous trace,

77
00:06:53.000 --> 00:06:58.286
bounded recursion, deterministic
rejection, verified side effects, and a

78
00:06:58.286 --> 00:07:03.571
typed return artifact. Test a correct
transfer plus wrong recipient,

79
00:07:03.571 --> 00:07:08.857
missing provenance, excessive permission,
poisoned context, timeout, recursive

80
00:07:08.857 --> 00:07:14.143
bounce, and unsafe output. Then run
adapter tests for each

81
00:07:14.143 --> 00:07:19.429
selected provider implementation,
including unsupported features and

82
00:07:19.429 --> 00:07:24.714
fallback behavior. Portability is proven
by equivalent contract outcomes and

83
00:07:24.714 --> 00:07:30.000
evidence, not common vocabulary or
matching SDK method names.

84
00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:36.000
Choose one workflow with triage,
specialist, reviewer, and human roles.

85
00:07:36.000 --> 00:07:42.000
Decide which transitions are delegation
and which transfer active control.

86
00:07:42.000 --> 00:07:48.000
Draft the packet fields, recipient
validation, context filter, authority map,

87
00:07:48.000 --> 00:07:54.000
budget, and return states.

88
00:09:24.000 --> 00:09:31.000
Checkpoint. The parent may publish
content, but the reviewer only

89
00:09:31.000 --> 00:09:38.000
needs to read evidence and comment. Should
the handoff include

90
00:09:38.000 --> 00:09:45.000
the parent's publish credential?

91
00:10:45.000 --> 00:10:50.250
Do not forward publish authority. Resolve
the reviewer under its

92
00:10:50.250 --> 00:10:55.500
own identity and grant only read and
comment access to

93
00:10:55.500 --> 00:11:00.750
the required objects. Record publish and
delete as denied actions.

94
00:11:00.750 --> 00:11:06.000
If the reviewer later proposes
publication, return that proposal to

95
00:11:06.000 --> 00:11:11.250
the authorized parent or a human approval
path. If you

96
00:11:11.250 --> 00:11:16.500
focused only on removing the publish tool
from the prompt,

97
00:11:16.500 --> 00:11:21.750
check the credential too; hidden or
accidental calls must still

98
00:11:21.750 --> 00:11:27.000
fail authorization. Context filtering and
permission enforcement must agree.

99
00:11:27.000 --> 00:11:34.000
Open the handoff contract activity. Define
four roles, create packet

100
00:11:34.000 --> 00:11:41.000
and return schemas, filter context, map
permissions, and run eight

101
00:11:41.000 --> 00:11:48.000
scenarios: correct transfer, wrong
recipient, missing provenance, excessive

102
00:11:48.000 --> 00:11:55.000
permission, poisoned context, timeout,
recursive bounce, and rejection. Save

103
00:11:55.000 --> 00:12:02.000
every acceptance, containment, retry, and
escalation trace.

104
00:15:03.000 --> 00:15:09.000
When ready, begin the knowledge check. You
will distinguish delegation

105
00:15:09.000 --> 00:15:15.000
from handoff, identify the packet
contract, minimize recipient authority,

106
00:15:15.000 --> 00:15:21.000
respond to rejected transfers, and
preserve product invariants across

107
00:15:21.000 --> 00:15:27.000
provider frameworks.

108
00:15:27.000 --> 00:15:32.333
Transfer a validated contract, not a
history dump. Preserve intent

109
00:15:32.333 --> 00:15:37.667
and trace, narrow context and authority,
require acknowledgment, bound failure,

110
00:15:37.667 --> 00:15:43.000
and verify every return.
